(LST-22 — a list element may itself be a list.
 Also covers: LST-23 (a nested list prints recursively with its brackets
 intact), LST-24 (`[1, [2, 3], "four"]` prints exactly as written),
 LST-25 (a homogeneous list-of-lists keeps the fast path and still prints
 recursively), LST-26 (the worked example of LANGUAGE.md:2386-2388),
 LST-27 (two-level extraction, LANGUAGE.md:2390-2391).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST-22.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   [1, [2, 3], "four"]
   [2, 3]
   [3, 4]
   [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
   [1, 2]
)
a list called nested is [1, [2, 3], "four"].
print nested.
print element 2 of nested.
a list called deep is [1, [2, [3, 4]], 5].
print element 2 of element 2 of deep.
a list called homogeneous is [[1, 2], [3, 4]].
print homogeneous.
print element 1 of homogeneous.
